  "foaf:name": "Galápagos Infinito Sailing Oceanic Classroom",
  "sdo:name": "Galápagos Infinito Sailing Oceanic Classroom",
  "sdo:description": "Galápagos Infinito reconnects local Galapagos children with the ocean and their natural heritage through experiential learning, fomenting connection, curiosity, awareness and stewardship. Every year, all 7th graders, 10-12 years old, across the four inhabited islands take to the sea in an “oceanic classroom,” complemented by coastal ocean connection workshops. These experiences integrate ocean literacy, cultural storytelling, and hands-on exploration to inspire stewardship and pride in the islands’ role as a living laboratory of the ocean. Our inter-sectorial approach brings together education, conservation, and tourism; and with local partners from the public and private sector we reach over 500 students every year. With academic partners ensuring rigorous evaluation, and future plans for a Polynesian-inspired sailboat as a cultural classroom, we offer an innovative model for restoring society’s relationship with the ocean and advancing UN Ocean Decade goals.",
